  "limitations": [
    "Smaller record budgets cap distinct authenticated (tree ID, physical record) pairs and do not support the full production worst-case diversity. Proof arrays remain fixed-width; fewer actual records alone do not reduce compiled constraints.",
    "The unified prototype retains two separately authenticated roots and shared canopy hashes per tree, verifies record tree selectors and query source identities, and preserves own-only provenance for escrow and mint settings.",
    "Subject-pool capacities remain unchanged, so this isolates record-pool consolidation/capacity changes rather than also reducing subject capacity.",
    "No encryption, SPP circuit integration, mixed-owner redesign, setup or Groth16 proof timing is measured here.",
    "New circuit keys and witness/SDK changes would be required. Prototype counts are not an optimal lower bound."
  ],
